  "summary": "In this 38-second talk published May 8, 2013, Jeanne Bliss argues that social media success hinges on operational reliability. She states that reliability across the front line, processes, and response times creates a trust-worthy customer experience, because your reliability is what gives customers a story to tell: \"in social media, your ability to be reliable is what gives your customers a story to tell.\" The talk highlights specific reliability touchpoints—quality of staff, process reliability, how long it takes to answer a phone, and cycle time to deliver the first review—and invites organizations to assess their current reliability to turn service consistency into a compelling social narrative.",
